# 🩵 Key Features
<h3> 1. AI Problem Generation</h3>
   
   NPCs present learning problems in real-time using the **OpenAI API**. Instead of simply retrieving pre-stored questions, 
   it automatically generates new problems that fit the context. This allows users to always encounter new questions even in the same situation, 
   reducing the boredom of repetitive learning and increasing immersion.
   <br>
   
   <img width="400" height="450"  alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dce52c45-a24f-48aa-a8a9-6bbdc237996e" />
   <img width="400" height="450" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae5babd0-3da7-41b6-9c21-d825bc76b1db" />

<h3> 2. Gamified Learning</h3>
   Solving problems is not just a simple quiz, but is connected to the quest progression. For example, an NPC might present a problem by saying, "If you solve this problem, you can get the key!" and when the user answers correctly, rewards or progress events occur. Through this, the learning process becomes a part of the game progression, naturally providing motivation and fun.
   <br>
   <img width="400" height="450" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7956b295-2f91-4c3d-8e3b-8f6009998e1a" />
   <img width="400" height="450" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec61500b-7e10-4e74-97fa-ecf19cfb756c" />


<h3> 3. Unit-by-Unit Learning Management</h3>
   Problems can be managed by dividing topics according to textbook units, such as Unit 1 and Unit 2. 
   This allows students to learn effectively step-by-step.
   
<h3> 4. Random Problem Provision</h3>
     Even within the same unit, the same questions do not always appear; instead, different problems are randomly generated every time. Thanks to this, students do not get bored even during repetitive learning and can encounter various problem types, thereby strengthening their problem-solving and application skills.
<br>
   <img width="800" height="450" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3c70413a-648a-4d55-8593-c466fdf7831f" />

# 🩵 Expected Effects & Application Fields

Currently, only 7th-grade (middle school 1st grade) math problems are applied for testing purposes, but there are plans to expand to various subjects and multiple grade levels in the future. Features such as **difficulty adjustment** and **learning achievement tracking** through learning record analysis will also be added. Students can experience immersive learning while solving tailored problems in a gaming environment, gaining effects such as self-directed learning habits, improved concentration, and enhanced learning motivation. These effects can be utilized to reduce the educational gap and provide equitable learning opportunities.

In addition, this system can be used as a **personalized learning tool for individual students** in schools and academies, helping both public and private education provide learning materials tailored to student levels and manage learning achievements. Furthermore, it can be used as a **data collection and analysis tool** for analyzing learning patterns and adjusting difficulty in education-related research institutes or learning data analysis fields.
